
' Data flow / column lineage (STYLE rule 17). Start from preambles/house.puml + this file.
' Processes are rounded boxes, stores are cylinders, externals are actors; tables whose columns
' matter are `entity` bodies, and a column-to-column flow is `src::col --> dst::col`.
' Look at every member edge in step 5: under ortho it can enter at the table's top edge instead of
' its row (reference § Data flow and column lineage).
allowmixing
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 70

title Data flow diagram for <system or table> (as-of date)

actor "Replace: external source" as ext
rectangle "Replace: 1. process" as p1
database "Replace: store" as store

entity "replace.source_table" as src {
  replace_key : type
  replace_amount : type
}
entity "replace.target_table" as dst {
  replace_key : type
  replace_total : type
}

ext -down-> p1 : Replace: sends rows (protocol)
p1 -down-> store : Replace: writes (SQL)
src::replace_key --> dst::replace_key : copied
src::replace_amount --> dst::replace_total : summed

legend right
  |= Mark |= Meaning |
  | actor | external source or sink |
  | rounded box | process (numbered as in the source) |
  | cylinder | data store |
  | table | table whose columns the flow names |
  | column line | the target column is derived from the source column |
endlegend
@enduml
